
<!-- JUMBOTRON SECTION -->
<div class="jumbotron p-2 m-0">
    <div class="container text-center align-items-center">
        <h3 class="text-warning font-weight-bold" id="heading">@ViewBag.Message</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="container d-flex align-items-end">
        @Html.ActionLink("Home", "index", "home", null, new { @class = "text-primary small font-weight-bold pr-2" })
        <a class="text-primary small font-weight-bold pr-2" id="Divisor1" href="#">/</a>
        @Html.ActionLink("Service", "service", "service", null, new { @class = "text-primary small font-weight-bold pr-2" })
        <a class="text-primary small font-weight-bold pr-2" id="link3" href="#">/</a>
        @Html.ActionLink("Maintenance", "maintenance", "service", null, new { @class = "text-primary small font-weight-bold pr-2" })
    </div>
</div>
<!-- END JUMBOTRON -->

<div id="page-content">

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-lg p-4 border text-justify">
            <h5 class="text-success text-left">IMPORTANCIA DE MANUTENÇÃO</h5>
            <p class="text-dark small">
                Good and effective maintenance regime is crucial for operation and overall realibility of the installed measurement system. It provides confidence in the measured
                values, and gives asssurance to owners and partners, that system is measuring correctly and within specified uncertainty limits.
            </p>
            <img src="~/img/Helicopter-Landing-SMALL-1.jpg" class="img-fluid mb-2" />
            <br>
            <div class="p-0 align-items-end">
                @Html.ActionLink("Want to know more contact us", "Contact","Home", null, new { @class = "btn btn-info btn-lg btn-block" })
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg p-4 border text-justify">
            <h5 class="text-success text-left">MIMO MAINTENANCE SERVICES</h5>
            <p class="text-dark small">
                We can provide full metering support to asset maintenance by supplying dedicated and trained metering personnel. Our technicians can provide full metering
                support to your assets by carrying out necessary preventive and corrective maintenance routines.
            </p>
            <p class="text-dark small">
                Preventive maintenance is carried out at planned schedules, whilst corrective maintenance addresses breakdowns and equipment failures, and generally
                requires restorative work to be carried out. Easy fixes can usually be corrected quickly, and on the site. Other, more difficult cases, take more time
                and require effective planning, and vendor support to be rectified.
            </p>

            <div class="d-flex justify-content-between border-regular">
                <a class="nav-link text-primary small text-left font-weight-bold" href="#pdata1" data-toggle="collapse" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pdata1">Provision of manpower</a>
                <a class="nav-link text-primary small font-weight-bold" href="#pdata1" data-toggle="collapse" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pdata1">▽</a>
            </div>
            <div class="collapse border border-primary collapse-bg text-left" id="pdata1">
                <p class="text-primary small pl-3 pr-3 pt-2">
                    Provision of experienced and trained metering personnel to onshore or offshore facilities.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="d-flex justify-content-between border-regular">
                <a class="nav-link text-primary small text-left font-weight-bold" href="#pdata2" data-toggle="collapse" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pdata2">Preventive Maintenance Routines</a>
                <a class="nav-link text-primary small font-weight-bold" href="#pdata2" data-toggle="collapse" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pdata2">▽</a>
            </div>
            <div class="collapse border border-primary collapse-bg text-left" id="pdata2">
                <ul>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Meter Verifications</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Meter zero checks</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Certification of primary meters</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Certification of densitometers</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Flow computer configurations checks</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Management of logbooks</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="d-flex justify-content-between border-regular">
                <a class="nav-link text-primary small text-left font-weight-bold" href="#pdata3" data-toggle="collapse" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pdata3">Corrective Maintenance Routines</a>
                <a class="nav-link text-primary small font-weight-bold" href="#pdata3" data-toggle="collapse" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pdata3">▽</a>
            </div>
            <div class="collapse border border-primary collapse-bg text-left" id="pdata3">
                <ul>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Equipment troubleshooting</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Determine root cause</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Primary instrument removal and repair</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Secondary instrument removal and repair</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <br>
            <h5 class="text-success text-left">ACTIVITY PLANNING</h5>
            <p class="text-dark small">
                Scheduling of rotas, general maintenance support and contact with vendors is handled by engineering team onshore. Depending on project requirements
                onshore engineers can be employed to take care of scheduling and planning acitivities.
            </p>
            <div class="d-flex justify-content-between border-regular">
                <a class="nav-link text-primary small text-left font-weight-bold" href="#pdata4" data-toggle="collapse" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pdata4">Scheduling & Planning Tasks</a>
                <a class="nav-link text-primary small font-weight-bold" href="#pdata4" data-toggle="collapse" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pdata4">▽</a>
            </div>
            <div class="collapse border border-primary collapse-bg text-left" id="pdata4">
                <ul>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Planning of technician's rotas</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Planning of preventive maintenance routines</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Planning of corrective maintenance routines</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Planning of Shutdown work scopes</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Compiling and reviewing maitenance procedures</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Raising work orders and notifications</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Estimation of required manpower hours</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Contact with vendors</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Reviewing and clearing audit items</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <br>
            <h5 class="text-success text-left">TURNAROUND MAINTENACE SCOPES</h5>
            <p class="text-dark small">
                Some maintenance work scopes may only be completed during yearly turnaround. Turnaround scopes are generally planned well in advance and require facility approval.
                Once approval is given, relevant spare parts and equipment must be identifed and purchased. Manning requirements are then allocated, and potential Vendor
                support identified.

            </p>
            <div class="d-flex justify-content-between border-regular">
                <a class="nav-link text-primary small font-weight-bold" href="#pdata5" data-toggle="collapse" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pdata5">Turnaround Work Scopes</a>
                <a class="nav-link text-primary small font-weight-bold" href="#pdata5" data-toggle="collapse" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pdata5">▽</a>
            </div>
            <div class="collapse border border-primary collapse-bg text-left" id="pdata5">
                <ul>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Integrated facility planning</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Identification of all shutdown work scopes</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Identification of material and man hours required</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">Vendor support requirements</li>
                    <li class="text-primary small p-1 mr-2">detailed planning</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
